  "note": "CFV1-THR — the single, append-only declaration of the OQ-14 capture-quality bars. A bar is declared once; a revision APPENDS a new dated entry (a higher seq, supersedes pointing at the entry it replaces) and the old entry stays. Editing an entry in place is refused three ways: `thresholds.py register` (the only change command) never mutates an existing entry; a raw hand-edit leaves the entry's stored hash stale, which `thresholds.py verify` reports; and `thresholds.py append-only-check --git-base <ref>` refuses any change to a committed entry even if its hash was re-forged. The scorer reads the active bars from here; THRESHOLD.md's bar tables are generated from here. Do NOT hand-edit and there is no reseal command: change a bar with `thresholds.py register --bar <b> --kind <field|edge> --value <v> --registered <YYYY-MM-DD> --reasoning <why>` (it appends and regenerates THRESHOLD.md). Bar values recorded 2026-09-20, before any capture was read (git history is the ordering proof).",
